# create-spack-development commands

Generated by `setup.py`: Spack {{ spack_version }} (`{{ sif_path }}`), packages from
`{{ packages_repo_dir }}` (branch `{{ packages_branch }}`). Run the scripts directly
from a login node, not via `sbatch`.

```bash
cd {{ repo_dir }}
ENV=<env>                                # a directory name under environments/

./new_env.py ${ENV} --constraint zen3    # create (--from <dir> copies a manifest)
./spack_build.py -e ${ENV}               # concretize -> install -> module refresh
./spack_concretize.py -e ${ENV}          # single steps: also spack_pkgs_install.py, spack_mod_refresh.py
./spack_shell.py -e ${ENV}               # interactive container shell, environment active

# inside the shell
spack add 'zlib@1.3'
spack spec
spack concretize -f && spack install && spack module tcl refresh -y
spack find

# use the modules
export MODULEPATH={{ outputs_dir }}/${ENV}/modules:${MODULEPATH}
module avail
```

Job scripts, logs and build results: `{{ build_results_dir }}`
